new_candidates.body:
`KinematicsPluginFactory::removeFwdKinPlugin` erases the group when its last solver is removed, and then reads the group through the erased iterator:

```cpp
  group_it->second.plugins.erase(solver_it);
  if (group_it->second.plugins.empty())
    fwd_plugin_info_.erase(group_it);                // group_it is invalidated here

  if (group_it->second.default_plugin == solver_name) // read through the erased iterator
    group_it->second.default_plugin.clear();          // write through it when the solver was the default
```

`kinematics/core/src/kinematics_plugin_factory.cpp:149–154` in 0.35.0 (:228–233 on `master`). `removeInvKinPlugin` has the same code at :209–214 (:288–293 on `master`).

This is undefined behaviour: the comparison reads freed memory, and when the removed solver was also the group's default, `clear()` writes into it. Found by reading the source.

## Reproduce

```cpp
#include <tesseract/kinematics/kinematics_plugin_factory.h>

int main()
{
  tesseract::kinematics::KinematicsPluginFactory factory;

  tesseract::common::PluginInfo info;
  info.class_name = "KDLFwdKinChainFactory";

  factory.addFwdKinPlugin("new_group", "only_solver", info);
  factory.setDefaultFwdKinPlugin("new_group", "only_solver");
  factory.removeFwdKinPlugin("new_group", "only_solver");  // erases the group, then reads and writes it
}
```

The same steps with `addInvKinPlugin` / `setDefaultInvKinPlugin` / `removeInvKinPlugin` reach the inverse kinematics copy.

## Suggested fix

Clear the default before the group can be erased, in both functions:

```cpp
  if (group_it->second.default_plugin == solver_name)
    group_it->second.default_plugin.clear();

  group_it->second.plugins.erase(solver_it);
  if (group_it->second.plugins.empty())
    fwd_plugin_info_.erase(group_it);
```

Version: tesseract 0.35.0; the code is unchanged on `master`.
